<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sichelgaita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1040–1090</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Sikelgaita, Sichelgaita of Salerno</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sichelgaita was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> princess, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guaimar-iv-of-salerno">Guaimar IV of Salerno</a>, who married the Norman leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-guiscard">Robert Guiscard</a> in 1058. She accompanied him on campaign, and Anna Komnene describes her riding armoured into battle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Dyrrhachium</a> in 1081. Her brother Gisulf II lost Salerno to her husband in 1077, and her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-borsa">Roger Borsa</a> succeeded Robert as Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>.</p></div>
